crates/segment (lightcraft-segment) ports the SAM 3 model code of Hugging Face Transformers
(https://github.com/huggingface/transformers, src/transformers/models/sam3 and sam3_tracker),
Copyright The HuggingFace Team and Meta Platforms, Inc., licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
The port was modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026): translated from Python/PyTorch to
Rust on candle and restructured; each ported file says so. Because of this, crates/segment is
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 only (LICENSE-APACHE), not under the MIT option.

The SAM 3 weights are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed with it. A user downloads
the facebook/sam3 checkpoint only when they choose to (in the app, or by hand), under Meta's SAM
License (https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3/blob/main/LICENSE), a separate, non-OSI
licence. See docs/ai-masks.md.

crates/segment/src/sam1.rs uses Candle's Segment Anything implementation (MIT OR Apache-2.0).
Portable packages may include the Apache-2.0 SAM 1 ViT-B weights, distributed by Kornia as
safetensors with the original Meta tensor values. See docs/sam1-model.md and
docs/licenses/SAM1-LICENSE.txt. The SA-1B dataset is not included.

crates/inpaint (lightcraft-inpaint) uses Hugging Face Candle's Stable Diffusion APIs
(https://github.com/huggingface/candle, MIT OR Apache-2.0). Its CLIP tokenizer is adapted
from crates/segment's Apache-2.0 port, modified in 2026 for Stable Diffusion's 77-token
context. crates/inpaint is therefore licensed under Apache-2.0 only (LICENSE-APACHE).
The SD 1.5 inpainting model weights are not distributed with LightCraft. Users download
them separately under CreativeML OpenRAIL-M; see docs/generative-fill.md.

crates/inpaint/src/klein_text.rs adapts Candle 0.9.2's Qwen3 implementation
(https://github.com/huggingface/candle, MIT OR Apache-2.0) into a bounded,
cancellable feature encoder for FLUX.2 Klein. The Rust adaptation omits unused
language-model layers and the output head. Klein model weights remain separate.

crates/inpaint/src/klein_transformer.rs ports Flux2Transformer2DModel from
Hugging Face Diffusers 0.38.0, Copyright 2025 Black Forest Labs, The HuggingFace
Team and The InstantX Team, licensed Apache-2.0. Modified by LightCraft
contributors (2026): Rust/Candle inference, bounded query-tiled attention and
cooperative cancellation. Public FLUX.2-klein-4B checkpoint revision
e7b7dc27f91deacad38e78976d1f2b499d76a294 is separately licensed Apache-2.0;
the current portable package does not include it.

crates/inpaint/src/klein_vae.rs implements the Diffusers AutoencoderKLFlux2
architecture and checkpoint naming using Candle's Stable Diffusion blocks
(MIT OR Apache-2.0). The reference architecture is from Hugging Face Diffusers
0.38.0 (Apache-2.0). The tokenizer is a Rust implementation of the public Klein
checkpoint's Qwen2 BPE configuration, using permissively licensed Rust Unicode
normalization and regular-expression libraries. No tokenizer assets or model
weights are committed to this repository.

crates/inpaint/src/klein_sampling.rs adapts the schedule, latent packing and
inpainting operations from Diffusers 0.38.0 Flux2KleinInpaintPipeline and
FlowMatchEulerDiscreteScheduler (Apache-2.0), Copyright 2025 Black Forest Labs,
The HuggingFace Team and The InstantX Team. Modified by LightCraft contributors
(2026) for bounded Rust/Candle inference and the pinned Klein 4B configuration.

crates/inpaint/src/migan.rs ports the MIT-licensed MI-GAN inference architecture
from Picsart AI Research (PAIR), Copyright (c) 2024, at revision
2b793c5ece43f4253e32d4afc257120a5deed6f5 of
https://github.com/Picsart-AI-Research/MI-GAN. The port translates the inference
operations to Rust/Candle and uses the author's fixed ONNX-export noise tensors.
Portable CUDA packages include converted MI-GAN weights from revision
406830d0fa60666da0071c342ad2fbc8f30c5c64 of
https://huggingface.co/andraniksargsyan/migan. Both upstream code and weights have
their own MIT licences; see docs/licenses/MI-GAN-LICENSE.txt and
docs/licenses/MI-GAN-LICENSE-WEIGHTS.txt. Conversion/provenance: docs/migan-model.md.

